acket is sold with a qr code  aiming of creating a community of people  who at the end of use but not earlier  than two years said  not to encourage a fast fashion they can  take back the jacket to the shop  and get a credit for the value of the  raw material which is inside  at this point the company will collect  the jackets and send them back  to aqua filler for recycling them  through the economy regeneration  system clearly it is very easy to  recycle this  this product is one single material you  don't have to spend money to separate  into different layers or to create  technologies  for the separation which sometimes are  very difficult  so as i said there are basically two  systems either to design  that are easy to decompose or to design  products that are made with one single  material of course recyclable infinitely  like econo is so let me conclude  with this hope for the future that  we envision a future when people begin  with the end in mind  which means that designers are able to  design products  choosing the right raw materials and the  right way of manufacturing  aiming at the end to recycle them  and engineers the same and of course  consumers have the possibility to choose  among all the beautiful products  available those  that are not creating a problem  but on the contrary representing a  solution  thank you  my name is raghu colley i'm head of  customer centricity  at leapfrog investments  during the course of my work i was  fortunate enough to visit  some of our customers in emerging  markets  there is a couple running a restaurant  on the outskirts of  jakarta who work hard  and their dream is to save up money to  make a pilgrimage  to mecca there's another couple  retired school teachers in sri lanka who  gave tuitions to school children in the  evening  to supplement their pension income  and there's this man a farmer in south  of india  who proudly showed up his various cards  and one of them is the card debit card  with which  he can draw money from an atm he said  he does not feel comfortable going to  the bank because  he looks poor he's illiterate and his  clothes are dirty  and the millions of people like this in  emerging markets  who work very hard and who have dreams  and aspirations  like all affairs they would like to have  their own house  they would like to grow the business  send their children to the university  take care of healthcare needs and become  self-sufficient  in their lifetime it's not easy for them  because it's very difficult to get loans  because they do not have  collaterals or documents and sometimes  most of them do not have and have the  basic insurance  leapfrog was founded 10 years ago to  provide  capital to financial and healthcare  services companies  in southeast asia and sub-saharan africa  who are serving low-income groups  today we have raised over 1.6 billion  dollars in capital  have 29 investments in 10 markets and  our companies together impact the lives  of over 200 million customers  and many of them are these low-income  groups  let me introduce a few of our companies  pasar police is a fintech company  in indonesia they partner with online  services companies  such as tokopedia traveloka and gocheck  to provide  contextual insurance with low premiums  if you're buying a smartphone on  tokopedia you might be offered a screen  protection insurance  at the point of checkout they use  automation  to simplify the process of buying as  well as the process of claiming  for the consumer soft logic is a life  insurance company in sri lanka  and one of the best known they have an  excellent agency network  and they recently launched micro  insurance  for rural areas in partnership with the  postal service  and they also have partnerships with  mobile operators  for micro insurance vora kgfs  is a microfinance company in india  they provide 500 to thousand thousand  dollar loans to  women and rural entrepreneurs  for their various business activities  another company which used to be a  microfinance company has become a bank  two years ago think air they now serve  urban as well as rural customers and  have a wide range of banking services  including digi banking and they serve  almost  2.5 million customers  for us profit for us impact means profit  with  purpose we not only deliver on the  financial returns expected of a private  equity company  but we also deliver on the  impact goals as well  we have our own proprietary methodology  to measure  impact called the firm but a simple and  tangible metric  is essential products and scale  essential products and services at scale  to  emerging consumers our companies  collectively  has delivered millions of loans  and remittances and  as well as savings products  and they've touched the lives of over  200 million customers  and have been cumulatively growing at  the range of at a rate of 54 percent in  terms of customer  breach  why is impact so important for  investment  it's not only does good for the society  but  also provides a tremendous business  opportunity  the millions of customers all in the  emerging markets  with young demography in asia and africa  when someone turns 18 or 20 then to the  job market  they take the first loan or buy the  first insurance product  they buy vehicles they get married they  have children  they send the children to school and  they grow their business  and also take care of the healthcare  needs along the way  they are on a journey from the current  state to become middle class  in their lifetime and in the process  they require many products and services  and which  which provides a tremendous opportunity  for our companies  to serve them and enable them in their  journey to become middle class  companies can maximize the value from  these customers  with a ruthless focus on customers  companies can expand to new markets by  identifying new customer segments  and unmet needs they can drive the  revenue growth  by launching new products and with  extensive  consumer testing it can reduce the cost  of  customer acquisition through digital  marketing companies can enhance  customer experience across all touch  points and increase the loyalty  using data sciences companies can  cross-sell products  and with digital engagement we can  retain customers  and build on brand equity using a  combination of all these levers  we can maximize the profit per customer  this requires cross-functional effort  from various departments  marketing i.t operations products and  strategy it requires orchestration  to support this customer-centric culture  and build capabilities in our companies  an area of customer experience  we've launched a multi-year program  called six launchpad  in this program about 11 companies  are participating and they're all  consumer facing companies  they learn about new methodologies  techniques and tools from  guest speakers as well as internal  expert team in areas  of digital experience customer  measurement customer journey  and other areas they undertake projects  of three to four months duration with a  sharp focus  on improving the customer experience  and we provide guidance and mentoring  for them  during the course of this project as  well as measure the impact on the  business  at the end of the projects  let me share with you a few examples of  this  one of our companies provides micro  insurance  micro enterprise loans to small  businesses in rural india  the company has mapped the customer  journey end-to-end  across for the loan disbursement process  one of the things we've learned  is that it takes almost about eight to  ten years or more for the customer to  get the money  and secondly it requires several visits  by the  loan officers to visit the customer to  obtain documents  or to very fondly of the business for  credit assessment purposes  the company has entirely redesigned the  process and  improved upon the customer credit  assessment  algorithms today the turnaround time for  loan disbursement has come down to four  days from the previous eight to ten days  and they're also able to process more  loans per month  lifro also developed a customer  experience  score measurement and a dashboard and  many of our companies have implemented  this  over 250 to 400 customers are called  every month  for for this score and it is  the dashboard shows a sample for an  insurance company  across all phases of the journey not  only do you get a score for each phase  but also for specific areas within that  particular journey  management monitors this on a monthly  basis and in areas where the score is  low such as  the areas marked in red they take  interventions to fix those  this is much better than waiting for the  survey  at the end of the year and then acting  on it because  you can intervene this on a regular  basis this has a tremendous impact  on many of our companies to improve  their operations  another company my life launched their  micro insurance through ussd a few years  ago  and after more than two years they only  had a few thousand users because the  product was simply difficult to use  on the usb interface  the company has used design experts to  redesign the interface completely  and test it extensively with the  consumers before launching  since the launch a few months ago there  has been tremendous growth and they now  have a more than 200 000 customers  with a month on month growth rate of 37  clearly design had a big impact on the  traction  for customers here  another company in nigeria developed  an app for the customers the previous  version of the app they had had only a  few thousand users after three or four  years of years  using ux design expertise this product  was launched  a few months ago and now they have all  more than 18 000 users  and it has a 4.5 rating on the google  store  every month thousands of customers view  the monthly statements for the pensions  and the transactions history this  reduced the  calls to the customer's support for  these statements which is to happen  previously as you can see from all these  examples  using design to improve the experience  of the customers had a tremendous impact  on the business performance if you're a  financial services company  government agency or any business for  that matter  and want to impact with  experience design here are a few  pointers  based on my journey with the leaf raw  for the last few years  i think first and foremost is to  identify a member of the senior  leadership team  as responsible for the customer  experience customer experience is not  necessarily the responsibility of a  single function in the company it cuts  across  all the company and requires  orchestration therefore  a leadership team member is required for  that  it's absolutely worthwhile to map the  customer journey for all products and  segments in  very detail from the customer point of  view and this will show up  many pain points the customers has which  are not  usually identified in the operational  processes which most companies have  it's very useful to measure customer  experience score on a monthly basis  rather than the end of the year because  it gives an opportunity  to make interventions and  finally i think there are capabilities  companies need to build  in the areas of digital experience  design  data sciences or behavioral sciences  initially it might be helpful to have  consultants helping  but eventually being used to become  internal capabilities  of the company creating  impact is hard work it takes time it  requires  strategic thinking and as investors  we have a long-term view on that  back here in singapore i also eat at the  hawker stalls  like most of the residents of singapore  and i had to withdraw money  from atm to pay at the hawker centers  because most of them  accepted the cash  and recently the government of singapore  along with support from design agencies  and other organizations  have rolled out cashless payment systems  for many of these hawkers who are  older generation who have difficulties  switching to digital platforms  on their own i was very surprised  a few days ago when i went to one of my  favorite talkers  that they have a qr code hanging there  and i could make a cashless payment  clearly experience design not only  impacts  the likelihoods of entrepreneurs like  this but also  the economy as well as the quality of  life  for consumers like me as well  thank you to mark we and the team  at design singapore council for giving  me this opportunity  to share my experiences
 

